cker News","score":5,"comments":16,"year":2011},{"title":"  AJAX Search: Is Google Sweating Bing Or Just Feeling The Need For Speed? ","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=793855","site":"Hacker News","score":11,"comments":8,"year":2009},{"title":"Banking on fuel-sweating flora","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1320929","site":"Hacker News","score":10,"comments":2,"year":2010},{"title":"Your Cardio Routine Is Making You Fat","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=6003544","site":"Hacker News","score":6,"comments":4,"year":2013},{"title":"America Isn't Sweating Climate Change","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48651003","site":"Hacker News","score":9,"comments":1,"year":2026},{"title":"Cardio Before or After Weights?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44251501","site":"Hacker News","score":8,"comments":1,"year":2025},{"title":"Show HN: Pelatra- an interactive mobile game to play while using cardio equipment","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=12819317","site":"Hacker News","score":8,"comments":1,"year":2016}],"web":[{"title":"Perspiration (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perspiration"},{"title":"Dehydration (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dehydration"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Facial fat & puffiness","chain":["Exercise raises sweat output","Fluid and sodium lost","Less puffy, leaner look"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Exercise increases sweat output, removing water and some sodium, so users look leaner and less puffy for a while afterward. The physiology of sweat is well known, and the effect on facial appearance has not been tested."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Sweating is the release of fluid by sweat glands, which in humans mainly regulates temperature. Heat and muscle exertion increase output, and sweat is mostly water with small amounts of sodium, potassium and other solutes.[1]","During average-intensity exercise water losses can reach about 2 litres per hour, and adults can sweat 2 to 4 litres per hour at peak.[1] In looksmaxxing contexts, cardio and sweating are described as a way to shed fluid for a leaner look. No studies on facial appearance were found in the sources reviewed."],"infobox":[["Type","Exercise-induced fluid loss"],["Sweat composition","Mostly water, about 0.2 to 1% solutes[1]"],["Typical exercise loss","About 2 L/hour in average-intensity exercise[1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Physiology","paras":["Eccrine glands cover much of the body and produce a watery secretion whose evaporation cools the skin. Daily water loss varies widely, from about 100 mL to 8,000 mL, and acclimatization increases the maximum sweat rate while lowering the salt concentration of sweat.[1]","Exercise in heat can cause sweat losses over 2 L/hour in competitive sport, which also depletes electrolytes such as sodium and may cause muscle cramps.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Perspiration","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perspiration","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Dehydration","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dehydration","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Cardio","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/cardio.1789503/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228083253/https://looksmax.org/threads/cardio.1789503/"},{"title":"Cardio is the highlight","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/cardio-is-the-highlight.1740852/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260224133651/https://looksmax.org/threads/cardio-is-the-highlight.1740852/"},{"title":"LifeFuel Cardio/weightlifing on coffee+ l theanine + asprin","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/cardio-weightlifing-on-coffee-l-theanine-asprin.543827/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220817062722/https://looksmax.org/threa